cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Mobile Stroke Unit placement — optimization models
message: >-
  For the coverage models, cite the article under preferred-citation. For BRAIN,
  cite the unpublished manuscript under references, which is under journal
  submission.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Markhorst
    given-names: Berend
repository-code: https://github.com/berendmarkhorst/MSU
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Solver-independent Pyomo implementations of the two Maximal Covering Location
  Problem variants used to optimize Mobile Stroke Unit placement: one with plain
  travel-time coverage and one that also allows an ambulance to rendezvous with
  the MSU en route. BRAIN jointly optimizes one MSU's base and dispatch radius
  to maximize expected health outcomes while accounting for vehicle unavailability.
keywords:
  - mobile stroke unit
  - facility location
  - maximal covering location problem
  - emergency medical services
  - operations research
  - pyomo
